==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|swëben}}, from {{inh|de|goh|swebēn}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*swibāną||to move}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*ksweybʰ-||to twist, turn around}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃveːbən/|[ˈʃveː.bm̩]|[-bən]}}
* {{audio|de|De-schweben.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|<sein,haben>}}

# to [[hover]], [[soar]], [[float]], [[drift]]

====Usage notes====
* The auxiliary is always {{m|de||sein}} when there is movement from one place to another: {{m|de||Die Drohne ist weiter nach Norden geschwebt.|The drone floated further towards the north.}} When there is no movement or movement within a confined space, the normal choice is {{m|de||haben}}, but {{m|de||sein}} is also possible: {{m|de||Die Drohne hat&thinsp;/&thinsp;ist über unsern Köpfen geschwebt.|The drone hovered above our heads.}}

====Conjugation====
{{de-conj|<sein,haben>}}

